<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Callicrates</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Callicrates was an Athenian architect of the fifth century BCE who designed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthenon">Parthenon</a> together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ictinus">Ictinus</a> in the building programme of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a>. He is also credited with the small Ionic Temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> Nike on the Acropolis and worked on the walls linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piraeus">Piraeus</a>.</p></div>
